    <IRS990ScheduleO documentId="RetDoc1044400001">
      <SupplementalInformationDetail>
        <FormAndLineReferenceDesc>FORM 990, PART VI, SECTION B, LINE 11B</FormAndLineReferenceDesc>
        <ExplanationTxt>TAX PREPARER PROVIDES A COPY OF THE DRAFT 990 TO THE ORGANIZATION. THE ORGANIZATION REVIEWS FORM 990 AND SEES THAT TAX PREPARER PROPERLY MAKES THE CHANGES. ANOTHER DRAFT IS PROVIDED TO THE ORGANIZATION AND THE PROCESS REPEATS UNTIL THE ORGANIZATION IS SATISFIED WITH THE RETURN. THE RETURN IS THEN FILED.</ExplanationTxt>
      </SupplementalInformationDetail>
      <SupplementalInformationDetail>
        <FormAndLineReferenceDesc>FORM 990, PART VI, SECTION B, LINE 12C</FormAndLineReferenceDesc>
        <ExplanationTxt>MEMBERS SIGN THE POLICY UPON ELECTION TO THE BOARD AND THIS CONCEPT IS REVIEWED AT THE ANNUAL BOARD MEMBER CONFERENCE.</ExplanationTxt>
      </SupplementalInformationDetail>
      <SupplementalInformationDetail>
        <FormAndLineReferenceDesc>FORM 990, PART VI, SECTION B, LINE 15</FormAndLineReferenceDesc>
        <ExplanationTxt>GOALS ARE SET ANNUALLY AND WRITTEN PERFORMANCE APPRAISALS ARE PREPARED. FOR THE EXECUTIVE DIRECTOR, THE BOARD OF DIRECTORS OBTAINS INDEPENDANT SALARY DATA AND SOLICITS PERFORMANCE INPUT FROM KEY STAKEHOLDERS. A WRITTEN REVIEW IS PREPARED AND DELIVERED IN PERSON BY THE PRESIDENT. THE INDEPENDANT DATA AND PERFORMANCE RATING ARE STUDIED TO DETERMINE THE NEW SALARY WHICH IS PROCESSED THROUGH PAYROLL. OTHER EMPLOYEES FOLLOW THE SAME PROCESS, WITH THE EXECUTIVE DIRECTOR RESPONSIBLE FOR THE REVIEW.</ExplanationTxt>
      </SupplementalInformationDetail>
      <SupplementalInformationDetail>
        <FormAndLineReferenceDesc>FORM 990, PART VI, SECTION C, LINE 19</FormAndLineReferenceDesc>
        <ExplanationTxt>GOVERNING DOCUMENTS &amp; FINANCIAL STATEMENTS AVAILABLE UPON REQUEST.</ExplanationTxt>
      </SupplementalInformationDetail>
    </IRS990ScheduleO>
